          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $0<r<R$ and $n\\ge 1$. Then there exists a smooth function $\\rho:\\mathbb R^n\\to [0,1]$ such that $\\rho=1$ on $\\overline B_r(0)$ and $\\operatorname{supp}(\\rho)\\subseteq B_R(0)$.",
