          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "If $K=\\varnothing$, set $\\chi_N=0$ for all $N$; the empty set is a neighborhood of $K$, so every assertion is vacuous. Assume henceforth $K\\ne\\varnothing$. For each $x\\in K$, choose concentric balls $B_{r_x}(x)\\Subset B_{R_x}(x)\\Subset U$. By [F1], take $b_x\\in C_c^\\infty(B_{R_x}(x))$ with $0\\le b_x\\le1$ and $b_x=1$ on $B_{r_x}(x)$. Compactness gives a finite subcover $B_{r_1}(x_1),\\ldots,B_{r_m}(x_m)$ of $K$. The smooth function\n$$\ng=1-\\prod_{j=1}^m(1-b_{x_j})\n$$\nsatisfies $0\\le g\\le1$, equals one on the open set $O=\\bigcup_{j=1}^m B_{r_j}(x_j)$ containing $K$, and has compact support $S\\Subset U$. This construction uses only finite subcover compactness.",
