          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U\\subset\\mathbb R^n$ be open, and let $K\\subset U$ be compact. There are constants $A,C>0$ and functions $\\chi_N\\in C_c^\\infty(U)$ for each integer $N\\ge1$ such that $0\\le\\chi_N\\le1$, $\\chi_N=1$ on a fixed neighborhood of $K$, and\n$$\n|\\partial^\\alpha\\chi_N(x)|\\le C(AN)^{|\\alpha|}\n\\qquad (x\\in\\mathbb R^n,\\ |\\alpha|\\le N).\n$$\nThese are smooth compact cutoffs; no compactly supported analytic function is asserted.",
