          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-compactly-supported-distributions-extend-to-smooth-functions",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Give $C^\\infty(\\Omega)$ the topology generated by $q_{K,m}(f)=\\max_{|\\alpha|\\le m}\\sup_K|\\partial^\\alpha f|$ for compact $K\\subseteq\\Omega$ and $m\\ge0$. A compactly supported distribution $u$ has a unique continuous complex-linear extension to this space, given by\n$$\\widetilde u(f)=u(\\chi f),$$\nwhere $\\chi\\in\\mathcal D(\\Omega)$ is any cutoff equal to one near $\\operatorname{supp}u$. The result is independent of $\\chi$. The extension vanishes on every smooth function zero near the support. No Hahn–Banach or choice axiom is needed.",
