      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Fix one real-analytic chart and two smooth cutoffs $\\chi,\\widetilde\\chi$ that both equal one on a neighborhood of the base point. Choose a smaller center neighborhood $U_0$ and a compact support neighborhood so that $|x-y|\\ge d>0$ whenever $x\\in U_0$ and $y\\in\\operatorname{supp}(\\chi-\\widetilde\\chi)$. By continuity in the fixed-support topology [F3], in either distributional type the pairing is bounded by $C_0$ times the maximum of finitely many derivatives of its test object; a coordinate density factor, when present, has bounded derivatives on the compact chart support. Those derivatives of $(\\chi-\\widetilde\\chi)e^{i\\lambda(x-y)\\cdot\\omega-\\lambda|x-y|^2/2}$ are bounded by $C_1(1+\\lambda)^m e^{-\\lambda d^2/2}$ uniformly for $x\\in U_0$, directions near $\\omega_0$, and $\\lambda\\ge1$. Since a polynomial times $e^{-\\lambda d^2/2}$ is bounded by $C_2e^{-c\\lambda}$ for any fixed $0<c<d^2/2$, replacing one fixed-chart cutoff by the other changes the FBI packet by an exponentially small term.",
