        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Thus the exponential-decay criterion is independent of the fixed-chart cutoff. The finite-order sequence [F2] supplies the uniform localizers required when a distribution is restricted to a smaller chart; it avoids any use of compactly supported analytic bumps. For a distributional density $V$ in the fixed chart, define the scalar distribution $u_V$ by $\\langle u_V,\\varphi|dy|\\rangle=\\langle V,\\varphi\\rangle$. Continuity follows from [F3], and the vanishing-open sets of $u_V$ and $V$ agree because $|dy|$ is nowhere zero, so their supports agree. The packet pairings agree by definition. Hence [F4]–[F5] give the local Euclidean tempered and smooth-function realizations for either distributional type. This proves the cutoff and localization clauses without a choice axiom.",
