          "claim": "Since $F$ is a submersion, its differential has rank $k$. The tangent space of its zero level is $T_{(g,x)}Z=\\ker DF(g,x)$. In finite-dimensional linear algebra, the annihilator of the kernel of a rank-$k$ linear map is the image of its transpose: inclusion follows from $\\tau^TDFv=0$ for $v\\in\\ker DF$, and both spaces have dimension $k$. Hence every conormal is uniquely $DF^T\\tau=(D_gF^T\\tau,D_xF^T\\tau)$.",
