          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $X$ be a real-analytic manifold, let $x_0\\in X$, and let $\\Sigma$ be a $C^2$ hypersurface through $x_0$, meaning that in a smooth local chart it is the graph of a $C^2$ function with nonzero conormal $\\nu_0\\in T^*_{x_0}X$. Let $f\\in\\mathcal D'(X)$ vanish on one side of $\\Sigma$ in a neighborhood of $x_0$, meaning that in such a chart its restriction is zero on either the strict epigraph or strict subgraph of that defining function. If either $(x_0,\\nu_0)\\notin\\operatorname{WF}_A(f)$ or $(x_0,-\\nu_0)\\notin\\operatorname{WF}_A(f)$, then $f=0$ in a neighborhood of $x_0$.",
